{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 3"},"body":"The three conjunctions align with the three displayed parts of thm:main.\n\nInspected: Read full challenge, coordinateDistance, GoodDimension, dimension and gamma; compared thm:main.","content_sha256":"sha256:3f7a3c09653f37fd0732fbd611d4aade188c46b79a03e95206749436399bd571","fingerprint":"sha256:e08d7ed341aaf5d2d5928adb18e6abd1d2061aa691a72495aaa530d7e6448e7c","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The three conjunctions align with the three displayed parts of thm:main.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:651ac125ea27b18d0e3d23077a6cc3a3824e3ecadecf59fe2e29e20f2280d397","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.SubpolynomialLp.source_main"],"explanation":"GoodDimension defines universal embeddings of n-point Lp configurations into finite coordinate Lp with distortion D and a positive scale. source_main gives the logarithmic lower and subpolynomial upper bounds for D>1, the exact-embedding quadratic bounds for n>=9, and the two logarithmic limits with the same piecewise gamma(p).","fingerprint":"sha256:f74980ef4aa5983dbf5faee82bb07036a6269c0d93676e0102c372a702d327e4","limitations":"The formal theorem additionally asserts the least dimension has GoodDimension; faithfulness of the universal-space representation is not independently certified.","relation":"same-claim","row_id":"Subpolynomial-dimension-reduction-in-Lp-September-23-2026#thm:main","statement_sha256":"sha256:e2bd361eaee849679afa0edea9758694a925029a418bf6d19c97bde987efb8e0"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance"